Subject: [PATCH 0004] shared heap: guarded-subrange read-only spans (Design B)

Hull extension. Adds a per-heap valid sub-window (valid_offset, valid_size) to a
pre-allocated shared heap so the guest can access only [valid_offset,
valid_offset + valid_size) inside the reserved [0, size) region, while native
backing = map_base and reserved size = map_len keep the whole reserved range
inside the live mmap. Placement/overlap stay keyed off the reserved size; only
the access bound moves. valid_size == 0 preserves full-heap behavior for every
existing (and runtime-managed) caller. See docs/wamr_shared_heap_guarded_subrange_design.md.

Files: core/iwasm/interpreter/wasm_runtime.h (WASMSharedHeap fields),
core/iwasm/include/wasm_export.h (SharedHeapInitArgs fields),
core/iwasm/common/wasm_memory.c (create validation, update_last_used bounds,
is_app_addr / is_native_addr valid sub-range, reset memset).
---
--- a/core/iwasm/interpreter/wasm_runtime.h
+++ b/core/iwasm/interpreter/wasm_runtime.h
@@ -111,6 +111,13 @@
     /* Hull ext: 1 = read-only mapped region; a WASM store into it traps
      * instead of writing. Only set for pre-allocated heaps. Default 0. */
     bool read_only;
+    /* Hull ext (0004): guarded subrange (Design B). The GUEST-accessible window
+     * is the valid sub-range [valid_offset, valid_offset + valid_size) inside
+     * the reserved [0, size) region; the slop prefix and page-rounding suffix
+     * are inaccessible. valid_size == 0 means the full heap (valid_offset == 0),
+     * so every existing / runtime-managed heap is unchanged. */
+    uint64 valid_offset;
+    uint64 valid_size;
 } WASMSharedHeap;
 
